# Lustra — frontend

## Structure (`apps/web`)

`app/` routes · `entities/` presentational domain UI · `features/` stateful scenarios · `shared/` api/hooks/ui/lib. Landing stays mostly static Astro islands.

## Naming

- Files/folders: **kebab-case** — `master-card.tsx`, `booking-sheet.tsx`, `use-hold-timer.ts`.
- Exported components/hooks: PascalCase / `use*` camelCase in source.
- Event handler **props** only: `onSubmit`, `onChange`. Internal functions / consts: `submitForm`, `handleChange` — never `on*` unless it is a prop.
- Prefer arrow functions for handlers declared inside components.
- **No negative margins** (`margin-top: -N`) — fix layout with flex/grid/gap/padding instead.

## Imports & CSS modules

- Use `@/` aliases **everywhere** (including same feature/module). Relative only for `./foo` next to the file if needed — prefer `@/features/...` / `@/modules/...`.
- Style via **CSS modules** with named classes (`.input`, `.radioInput`) — never nest tags (`.field input`, `.steps li`).
- **Never** use `:global(...)` to override shared classes.
- **Never** use inline `style={{ ... }}` — tokens + CSS modules only.
- Layout chrome (shell/header/nav/brand): shared CSS-module component — don’t mix global `.shell` / `.site-header` in some pages and modules in others.

## Components

- **One React component per `.tsx` file** (plus its props type). If you split a child out of a shell — new kebab-case file (`calendar-body.tsx`), not a second `function` in the same module. Tiny private render helpers that are not components are still forbidden in `ui/` if they are JSX-returning components.
- **≤ 300 lines**; split into composed children + hooks.
- Composition over props-drilling mega-components.
- **No render props** (`children={(x) => ...}`). Prefer context, hooks, or plain `children: ReactNode`.
- Four UI states where data loads: `loading` (skeleton), `empty`, `error` (+ retry), `success`.
- No cards in hero; avoid generic dashboard chrome on marketing/public pages.
- Shared interactive UI (`Button`, …) from `shared/ui` — never raw `btn btn-primary` string classes in features.
- **No nested ternaries in JSX** — extract a small child component (own file) or early `if` returns.
- **Pure helpers never live inside UI components** (`ui/*.tsx`). Put them in `model/` or `shared/lib/` (kebab-case file) and import. Same for date/money/formatters and form mappers.

```ts
// ❌ BAD — util buried in the component file
export function BlockDialog() {
  function buildIsoRange(...) { ... }
  return <form />
}

// ❌ BAD — two components in one file
export function CalendarShell() { ... }
function CalendarBody() { ... }

// ✅ GOOD
// model/build-block-iso-range.ts
export function buildBlockIsoRange(...) { ... }

// ui/calendar-body.tsx
export function CalendarBody() { ... }

// ui/calendar-shell.tsx
import { CalendarBody } from '@/features/master-calendar/ui/calendar-body'
import { buildBlockIsoRange } from '@/features/master-calendar/model/build-block-iso-range'
```

## State & effects

- Server/public data: RSC + `fetch` tags / TanStack Query for private mutable data.
- Filters/steps: URL `searchParams` as source of truth.
- Forms: react-hook-form + Zod from `@lustra/contracts`.
- **Avoid `useEffect`** unless syncing with an external system (DOM, browser API, non-React widget). Prefer:
  - derived state during render
  - event handlers
  - `useEffectEvent` when an effect must call latest callback
  - Query/`useSyncExternalStore` for subscriptions
- No global client store by default (no Zustand unless offline).

## Validation & roles

- Client validation = UX only. Never skip API checks.
- Gate routes by role (`client` / `master` / `admin`); never trust hidden buttons alone.

## Tests

- Unit-test pure utils in `shared/lib` and feature helpers (Vitest).
- E2E (Playwright) for critical flows — see testing skill.
